==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|gingle}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{lb|en|onomatopoeia}}; compare {{m|en|jangle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒɪŋɡəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-jingle.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋɡəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The sound of [[metal]] or [[glass]] clattering against itself.
#: ''He heard the '''jingle''' of her keys in the door and turned off the screen.''
# {{lb|en|music}} A small piece of metal attached to a musical instrument, such as a [[tambourine]], so as to make a [[jangling]] sound when the instrument is played.
#: ''Her tambourine didn't come with any '''jingles''' attached.''
# {{lb|en|advertising}} A memorable short [[song]], or in some cases a [[snippet]] of a popular song with its [[lyrics]] modified, used for the purposes of advertising a [[product]] or [[service]] in a [[television|TV]] or [[radio]] [[commercial]].
#: ''That used-car dealership's '''jingle''' has been stuck in my head since we heard that song.''
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=June 3, 2012
|author=Nathan Rabin
|title=TV: Review: THE SIMPSONS (CLASSIC): “Mr. Plow” (season 4, episode 9; originally aired 11/19/1992)
|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/mr-plow,75560/
|page=
|passage=The best of friends become the worst of enemies when Barney makes a hilarious attack ad where he viciously pummels a cardboard cut-out of Homer before special guest star Linda Ronstadt joins the fun to both continue the attack on the helpless Homer stand-in and croon a slanderously accurate, insanely catchy '''jingle''' about how “Mr. Plow is a loser/And I think he is a boozer.”}}
# A [[carriage]] drawn by [[horse]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1916|passage=They drove in a '''jingle''' across Cork while it was still early morning and Stephen finished his sleep in a bedroom of the Victoria Hotel.|author=[[w:James Joyce|James Joyce]]|title=[[w:Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man|Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man]]|published=Macmillan Press Ltd|page=85}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A brief phone call; a [[ring]].
#: ''Give me a '''jingle''' when you find out something.''
# A [[jingle shell]].
# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} [[coin|Coin]] [[money]].
#* '''2004''', ''{{w|Penn & Teller: Bullshit!}}'', "P.E.T.A." (season 2, episode 1)
#*: If all you folks who donate your hard-earned '''jingle''' to PETA aren't convinced of your ill-advised ways yet, you should probably check this out.

